    <a href="/archives">Archives</a>
    <a href="/sections">Sections</a>
    <a href="/operators">Operators</a>
  </div>
  <div class="main">
    <div><hr/></div>
    <div style="margin:20px;">
    <h1>Welcome to NetLog!</h1>
    <p>NetLog allows you to log participation in nets, training and public service events
    <div class="line" style="margin:0px"><hr/></div>
    </div>

  <div class="grid-container">
    <div class="grid-item">
      <h2>Current information</h2>
      <p>
      <br>Total sections - {{sectionCount}}
      <br>Total operators - {{operatorCount}}
      <p>Recurring events - {{recurringEventsCount}}
      <p>Active events - {{activeEventsCount}}
    </div>
    <div class="grid-item">
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <p>Create an ARRL ARES section and add operators to it.
      <p>Create a recurring event (net, training, etc) and create a active event from it for a date and time. 
      <p>Then add participants to that active event when they check-in or out.
      <p>Once you secure that active event, you can view it in the Archives.
      <p>From the archives, you can generate reports useful to ARRL and your section.
    </div>
  <!-- end grid -->
